      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The fact that your symptoms alleviate once you're seated could indeed suggest something like gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD), which involves stomach acid irritating your esophagus, particularly when lying down or sitting up after a meal. However, considering your concern and since this burning sensation occurs while engaging in activities like walking stairs, it is important not to self-diagnose, especially further complicating it with considerations of heart issues. Monitoring your symptoms and discussing them with a healthcare professional would be the safer course of action. They can give you a more specific analysis and advice tailored to your situation, taking into account your lifestyle, stress levels, and any other relevant factors. Something urgent like severe chest pain would always warrant immediate medical attention. Until then, try to manage discomfort with the least amount of antacids needed, and be proactive about seeking professional medical advice.",
